Requests and console of the browser while deleting a unit of equipment from its page
(`repro.test.ts`, CPU throttled 8x during the delete). Times from the start of the test.

Before the workaround: the form's redirect runs `_goto(redirect, { refreshAll: true })`. Between
the POST's answer and the navigation, the page being left asks again for every query it renders,
the deleted unit's four among them (each answers 404), and Svelte warns about a derived of a
destroyed effect.

--- ZZ-SLOT-1: delete
5789ms POST deleteEquipment
5877ms GET getTheme
5877ms GET getMode
5877ms GET getCurrentTenant
5877ms GET getCurrentUser
5877ms GET getEquipment
5877ms GET getServiceHistory
5877ms GET getSubjectActivity
5877ms GET getUnitCoverage
5928ms console.warning: [svelte] derived_inert
  Reading a derived belonging to a now-destroyed effect may result in stale values
  https://svelte.dev/e/derived_inert
6070ms nav http://localhost:57656/equipment
6098ms GET getEquipmentList
6098ms GET getEquipmentFacets
6637ms GET getTableViews

After the workaround (the delete dialog submits with `submit().updates()`, so no refreshAll): only
the list it lands on loads.

--- ZZ-SLOT-1: delete
5409ms POST deleteEquipment
5542ms nav http://localhost:58071/equipment
5563ms GET getEquipmentList
5563ms GET getEquipmentFacets
6261ms GET getTableViews

When the 404 of getUnitCoverage arrives before the old page is destroyed (under load), the
contracts module's slot on that page logs (from e2e/orders.test.ts in a loaded full run):

error: The contracts/orders.detail.side/coverage contribution failed {status: 404, message: Order ORD-2026-00754 not found}
